A Floor Counter, a play in one act.

Romeo, the floor the elevator is on.
Juliet, the instruction that was just read.


Act I: Following the instructions.

Scene I: Step onto the elevator.

[Enter Romeo and Juliet]

Scene II: Read the next character.

Romeo:
 Open your mind!

Romeo:
 Is Juliet worse than nothing?

Juliet:
 If so, let us proceed to scene III.

Romeo:
 Is Juliet better than the sum of a big big big big big cat and a big big big cat?

Juliet:
 If so, you are as villainous as the difference between thyself and a cat.

Romeo:
 Is Juliet as good as the sum of a big big big big big cat and a big big big cat?

Juliet:
 If so, you are as handsome as the sum of thyself and a cat.

Juliet:
 Let us return to scene II.

Scene III: The last floor.

Juliet:
 Open your heart!
